Production Improvements I'd Add
For a real LINOOP deployment, I'd also add:
•	SQLite database to track provisioning state 
•	Retry logic for Zoom/cPanel API failures 
•	Username collision checking against AD 
•	Department-based AD OU placement 
•	Automatic group membership assignment 
•	Password-protected credential export 
•	Dry-run mode (--check) 
•	Rollback mode (--delete-user) 
•	Web dashboard for HR uploads 
That would give you an onboarding platform capable of handling hundreds or thousands of users reliably, with a single CSV upload as the entry point.




MANGING SLACK AUTOMATION:
For the Slack Free plan, there is an important limitation:
You cannot fully automate Slack user provisioning through supported Slack admin APIs. Those APIs are available only on higher-tier plans.
However, you can absolutely integrate Slack into your onboarding platform in a way that feels automated from the HR perspective.
